; Cracked-earth fissures radiating from the altar — adds a "site of
; ritual heat" feel without resorting to fire imagery (Westmoor owns
; the flame). Each fissure is a thin dark rectangle at a diagonal
; offset, none aligned with cardinal directions so they don't block
; sightlines from exits.
